{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/892636-how-do-you-handle-beings-that-acquire-a-template-during-play","id":892636,"title":"How do you handle beings that acquire a template during play?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-17T11:10:00-07:00","id":892636,"title":"How do you handle beings that acquire a template during play?","content":"I'm asking for how everyone runs their games, not interpretations of the official rules.<br /> <br /> Do you just apply 'Step Five' of the appropriate splat's character creation rules? If so, how do you roleplay the sudden manifestation of their abilities (Disciplines, Gifts, etc)? If not, what do you do? Do you give them the three extra merit dots? Do you <i>not</i> give them something that a 'starting' character of the splat would normally have?<br /> <br /> I'm even more interested in how thoroughly you play out the process of learning what it is to be a monster. Do the players run through lessons given by their sires on how to not drain somebody dry, or where to find the best places to feed without infringing on the territory of others? Do they know it instinctually?<br /> <br /> What about the intricacies of spirit politics for a new werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:50:35-07:00","id":892927,"title":"","content":"Well, just applying 'Step Five' works good enough for me. From there on, it depends a lot on the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Usually, if I do this, there's a story already going on, and it won't stop for the characters to get used to the new condition. In that case:<br /> 1- I explore the ignorance of the characters. Some things are instinctual, but most are not. Even instinctual things don't came with an understanding of said instincts.<br /> 2- The less instinctual abilities are learned in the way most interesting for the chronicle. Sometimes there are mentors already present in the chronicle, others the easier powers, like in-clan Disciplines, are more instinctive, but also their learning is cause of trouble and wonder.<br /> 3- Merits are a special case. If the chronicle is intended for the characters to deal a lot with supernatural critters, or become them, I'll probably give them 10 merit points from the start anyway. But probably not give them more Merit points later. The lack of supernatural merits will be a part of their condition as &quot;fresh meat&quot;.<br /> <br /> If there is more of an interest in making downtime for the characters to get used to powers, some of those change:<br /> 1- Whatever doesn't seem fun for the chronicle to explore the process is learned &quot;behind the curtains&quot;. A quick description covers whatever is relevant in the process, like owed favors.<br /> 2- If something is still fun to explore as not yet learned, it is noted so.<br /> 3- Probably the characters won't get more Merit points, instead following like above, but I would let them change dots of Merits around to represent the changes during downtime. Sometimes a player chooses to not spend dots at character creation to reserve them for this point, I have nothing against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}